<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - IMSA started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - IMSA started.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.P. Morgan said analyst Michael Gambardella had started coverage of Mexican steel company Grupo IMSA SA with a rating of buy.</p>
<p>In a May 21 report, he wrote, &quot;Grupo IMSA represents everything we like in a company: leading market positions, world-class facilities, highly variable cost structure, strong balance sheet, a high-growth market and a highly motivated management.&quot;</p>
<p>He estimated 1997 earnings per share at $2.97 and at $2.04 next year.</p>
<p>Gambardella set an 18-month target price of $30 for IMSA's American Depositary Receipts (ADRs). They were off 1/4 at 25 in New York.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
